# Fix bugs in desktop + web

When the user reports an issue or bug, fix it for **both** targets unless they say otherwise.

## Shared UI (fix once)

Most editor/UI logic lives in `desktopApp/src/renderer/src/` and is reused by the web app via the `@renderer` alias in `webApp/vite.config.ts`. Changes there apply to **both** desktop and web after rebuild/redeploy.

Examples: `LogoEditor`, `FaviconEditor`, `IconPaintEditor`, `useVersions`, `types`, renderer utils.

## Web-only (fix separately when relevant)

- `webApp/src/platform/api.ts` — `window.api` polyfill
- `webApp/src/platform/auth.ts`, `WebShell`, login/admin/templates UI
- `webApp/vite.config.ts`, `nginx.conf`, root `Dockerfile`, `server/`

## Desktop-only (fix separately when relevant)

- `desktopApp/src/main/` — Electron main process, IPC, file system, templates folder watcher
- `desktopApp/src/preload/`

## Checklist after a user-reported bug

1. Identify whether the bug is shared renderer, web-only, desktop-only, or server.
2. Apply the fix in every layer that applies (not just one).
3. Do not leave divergent behavior between desktop and web for the same feature unless intentionally platform-limited.
